$ # the frame every model tool derives, and what each does when the file lies
$ python3 tools/_model_shape.py templates/onnx-inference-ofx/models/test_shape.txt
1x3x48x64xf32
exit=0

$ printf "3 48\n" > /tmp/bad-shape.txt && python3 tools/_model_shape.py /tmp/bad-shape.txt
/tmp/bad-shape.txt must hold "channels height width", found [3, 48]
exit=2

$ # model_probe: the committed model (dynamic H/W) takes its frame from the fixtures
$ tools/model_probe.py templates/onnx-inference-ofx/models/test_conv.onnx
model        test_conv.onnx  (611 B, sha256 87f145d8da98f00d, opset 17 IR 8)
input        input  tensor(float)  [1, 3, h, w]
output       output  tensor(float)  [1, 3, h, w]
channels     3  (from the model)
frame        64x48  (from test_shape.txt)
size         1x1 - output matches the input
dynamic H/W  yes - sizes are not fixed by the export
alignment    63 ok, 72 ok, 80 ok, 96 ok  => multiple of 1

$ # control: a model with a fixed 1x3x48x64 input, fed to the OLD probe (default 64x64)
error: the model did not run at 64x64: [ONNXRuntimeError] : 2 : INVALID_ARGUMENT : Got invalid dimensions for input: input for the following indices
exit=1

$ # and to the new one: it uses the model's own size
channels     3  (from the model)
frame        64x48  (from the model)
size         1x1 - output matches the input

$ # control: --size that the model cannot honour is named and ignored
channels     3  (from the model)
frame        64x48  (from the model)
             --size ignored: this model only runs at its own size

$ # control: a test_shape.txt that contradicts the model
error: the model fixes dimension 1 at 3, /tmp/static/test_shape.txt says 4
exit=2

$ # aot-compile-model.sh: the spec now comes from test_shape.txt
== run: CPU artifact on the committed input (1x3x48x64xf32, from test_shape.txt)
EXEC @test_conv
   max |difference| = 5.96e-08
   the ahead-of-time artifact reproduces the golden
exit=0

$ # control: test_shape.txt claiming width 65 (input is 48x64)
/tmp/aotctl/test_input.bin: 36864 bytes, 3x48x65 float32 needs 37440
aot: the committed input does not match test_shape.txt
exit=1
